WEBVTT

1
00:00:18.303 --> 00:00:20.073
[♪ lively music playing]

2
00:00:24.448 --> 00:00:27.353
Can we light some candles
or something. you know?

3
00:00:27.354 --> 00:00:30.560
Make it a little more romantic.
Since this is a double date?

4
00:00:30.561 --> 00:00:33.132
-Ooh. that's a nice idea.
-[Susan] Thanks.

5
00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:34.869
[Bret] I'd like to keep
the lights on.

6
00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:39.110
And maybe we should. you know.
move the party inside.

7
00:00:39.111 --> 00:00:41.114
[Thom] Why?

8
00:00:41.115 --> 00:00:43.520
The home invasions. There was
another one last Sunday night.

9
00:00:43.521 --> 00:00:47.126
And the houses were dark when
the home invasions happened?

10
00:00:47.127 --> 00:00:49.264
I mean.
that's why people broke in?

11
00:00:49.265 --> 00:00:52.403
I don't know. but I'm assuming
with the lights on. it's a deterrent.

12
00:00:52.404 --> 00:00:53.439
A deterrent.

13
00:00:54.241 --> 00:00:56.345
-A deterrent.
-Whoever is doing it

14
00:00:56.346 --> 00:01:00.319
also steals people's pets.
their cats. their dogs.

15
00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:01.756
Uses them ritualistically.

16
00:01:01.757 --> 00:01:03.425
[stammers]
Do you remember. Susan.

17
00:01:03.426 --> 00:01:05.664
the school mascot
on the first day of school?

18
00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:08.302
-Cult.
-Another girl is missing. too.

19
00:01:08.303 --> 00:01:10.608
-Who?
-Julie Selwyn from Marymount.

20
00:01:11.109 --> 00:01:13.412
It's been almost eight weeks
since she disappeared.

21
00:01:13.413 --> 00:01:15.249
Maybe she just ran away.

22
00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:18.523
Okay. guys. let's stop trying
to creep ourselves out.

23
00:01:18.524 --> 00:01:20.327
I wanna talk about the party.

24
00:01:22.599 --> 00:01:24.401
-The party?
-Yes.

25
00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:27.407
I'm going to throw a party
for Robert Mallory.

26
00:01:28.309 --> 00:01:30.647
It's going to be at my house.

27
00:01:30.648 --> 00:01:32.918
and I think we should all throw it
together. the four of us. to welcome him.

28
00:01:32.919 --> 00:01:35.222
And we'll invite everyone
in our senior class.

29
00:01:35.223 --> 00:01:38.731
-[Thom] Totally awesome.
-Cool. Fun. Love it. [sniffs]

30
00:01:39.498 --> 00:01:40.568
Wait. why?

31
00:01:41.302 --> 00:01:43.205
Why throw him a party?

32
00:01:43.206 --> 00:01:45.342
I think we should
make him feel welcome.

33
00:01:45.343 --> 00:01:49.118
I think he had some hard times.
and I think he needs to feel welcome.

34
00:01:50.621 --> 00:01:51.857
Hard times?

35
00:01:53.426 --> 00:01:55.196
What were the hard times?

36
00:01:55.564 --> 00:01:56.867
[♪ tense music playing]

37
00:02:00.273 --> 00:02:02.811
I was in Principal Croft's
office yesterday...

38
00:02:02.812 --> 00:02:05.884
He spent some time in a
developmental center working on his...

39
00:02:05.885 --> 00:02:08.923
[Susan] <i>Dr. Croft asked me
to throw this party.</i>

40
00:02:08.924 --> 00:02:10.861
<i>He said he was worried
about Robert</i>

41
00:02:10.862 --> 00:02:13.566
<i>and that my responsibility
as student body president</i>

42
00:02:13.567 --> 00:02:16.405
<i>was to make everyone feel
as welcome as possible.</i>

43
00:02:16.406 --> 00:02:17.608
I totally agree.

44
00:02:18.076 --> 00:02:20.413
-It seems that...
-What?

45
00:02:20.414 --> 00:02:23.419
Robert was institutionalized.

46
00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:25.624
In an asylum?
You've got to be kidding me.

47
00:02:25.625 --> 00:02:28.596
Croft said it was more
of a developmental center.

48
00:02:28.597 --> 00:02:30.934
He was treated for depression
and some other issues.

49
00:02:30.935 --> 00:02:33.573
Great. So the guy's been
locked away in a loony bin.

50
00:02:33.574 --> 00:02:36.546
That's a little dramatic. Bret.
You always embellish everything.

51
00:02:36.547 --> 00:02:39.384
-I'm a writer. It's my job.
-Look. no biggie.

52
00:02:39.385 --> 00:02:40.987
The guy went through some shit.

53
00:02:40.988 --> 00:02:45.262
his parents' divorce and
whatnot. his mother's death.

54
00:02:45.263 --> 00:02:46.432
I feel sorry for him.

55
00:02:48.369 --> 00:02:51.876
Robert Mallory needs a friend
and I intend to be one.

56
00:02:51.877 --> 00:02:53.378
-Me too.
-Me three.

57
00:02:53.379 --> 00:02:55.550
[Debbie] Wanna toot. Thommy?

58
00:02:55.551 --> 00:02:57.654
[Thom] No thanks. Debs. I gotta
get up early tomorrow to practice.

59
00:02:57.655 --> 00:02:59.792
-[Debbie] So that'll keep your body tight?
-I'm already tight.

60
00:02:59.793 --> 00:03:02.531
-I'm keeping it tight.
-You know what? I feel like some red wine.

61
00:03:02.532 --> 00:03:04.668
-Anyone for a nice cab?
-Please.

62
00:03:04.669 --> 00:03:06.906
He's a liar. guys.

63
00:03:06.907 --> 00:03:09.444
He lied about seeing me
at the movie theater

64
00:03:09.445 --> 00:03:12.483
last summer during <i>The Shining.</i> I do
not trust him and neither should you.

65
00:03:12.484 --> 00:03:15.590
Bret. it's just a party.

66
00:03:15.591 --> 00:03:17.493
No. Susan. it's a validation.

67
00:03:17.494 --> 00:03:20.432
Hey. guys. it's getting
a little tense in here.

68
00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:24.340
-Maybe we should hot-tub it.
-[gasps] Let's hot-tub it. Come on.

69
00:03:24.341 --> 00:03:26.278
-Let's go to the hot tub. Okay? Come on.
-[screams]

70
00:03:26.279 --> 00:03:27.314
Come on. [chuckles]

71
00:03:27.749 --> 00:03:29.485
[♪ playful music playing]

72
00:03:35.665 --> 00:03:39.238
<i>♪ Jesus ♪</i>

73
00:03:40.842 --> 00:03:43.011
<i>♪ Another day goes by ♪</i>

74
00:03:43.012 --> 00:03:44.248
[Debbie screams]

75
00:03:45.083 --> 00:03:46.987
[Debbie. Susan giggling]

76
00:03:50.828 --> 00:03:52.899
[no audible dialogue]

77
00:03:57.542 --> 00:04:02.416
[chuckles] Look.
we were in a mall. Remember?

78
00:04:02.417 --> 00:04:03.754
-[twig snaps]
-[Susan] No.

79
00:04:07.695 --> 00:04:08.730
[owl hooting]

80
00:04:10.501 --> 00:04:11.536
Oh. no.

81
00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:13.673
What's that? The killer?

82
00:04:13.674 --> 00:04:15.342
[Debbie. Susan laugh]

83
00:04:15.343 --> 00:04:16.378
[Thom laughs]

84
00:04:16.813 --> 00:04:19.051
Bret. please become a wino.

85
00:04:19.485 --> 00:04:22.658
You are so much more fun
when you drink. [chuckles]

86
00:04:22.659 --> 00:04:25.496
Okay. so we'll do a Saturday.

87
00:04:25.497 --> 00:04:27.634
My house. Robert's party.

88
00:04:27.635 --> 00:04:29.939
-It's settled. Settled.
-It's settled.

89
00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:31.742
-What?
-Scheduled. [chuckles]

90
00:04:31.743 --> 00:04:33.913
Guys. just to state the facts.

91
00:04:33.914 --> 00:04:36.017
He followed me to the mall.

92
00:04:36.018 --> 00:04:40.594
That's funny because he told me
that you were the one following him.

93
00:04:42.599 --> 00:04:44.879
-How do you know? Did you talk to him?
-[Susan chuckles]

94
00:04:48.476 --> 00:04:50.379
[♪ "Don't You Want Me" playing]

95
00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:52.718
-[Debbie gasps. chuckles]
-Oh. my God!

96
00:04:52.719 --> 00:04:56.058
I love this song. [shrieking]

97
00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:01.535
[laughs]

98
00:05:01.536 --> 00:05:02.839
Turn it up!

99
00:05:04.475 --> 00:05:07.347
Whoo. Go. Susan.

100
00:05:09.686 --> 00:05:13.025
Are we getting a show? Whoo.

101
00:05:13.026 --> 00:05:15.797
Yes! Susan.

102
00:05:15.798 --> 00:05:17.901
Oh. Thom. You're in for it.
You're in for it.

103
00:05:17.902 --> 00:05:19.606
-Prepare.
-She's right behind me?

104
00:05:21.175 --> 00:05:23.881
[Debbie] Oh. [chuckles]

105
00:05:24.583 --> 00:05:28.856
<i>♪ Now five years later on
You've got the world At your feet ♪</i>

106
00:05:28.857 --> 00:05:32.063
<i>♪ Success has been
So easy for you ♪</i>

107
00:05:32.064 --> 00:05:33.099
Come.

108
00:05:34.201 --> 00:05:36.338
Come on. give us choreography.

109
00:05:37.074 --> 00:05:38.409
[Susan giggling]

110
00:05:41.415 --> 00:05:44.689
<i>♪ Don't. don't you want me? ♪</i>

111
00:05:45.223 --> 00:05:49.632
<i>♪ You know I can't believe it
When I hear that You won't see me ♪</i>

112
00:05:49.633 --> 00:05:52.905
<i>♪ Don't. don't you want me? ♪</i>

113
00:05:53.373 --> 00:05:57.814
<i>♪ You know I don't believe you
When you say that You don't need me ♪</i>

114
00:05:57.815 --> 00:06:01.756
<i>♪ It's much too late to find You
think you've changed Your mind ♪</i>

115
00:06:01.757 --> 00:06:06.031
<i>♪ You'd better change it back
Or we will both be sorry ♪</i>

116
00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:09.104
<i>♪ Don't you want me. baby? ♪</i>

117
00:06:10.473 --> 00:06:13.946
<i>♪ Don't you want me? Oh ♪</i>

118
00:06:13.947 --> 00:06:17.487
<i>♪ Don't you want me. baby? ♪</i>

119
00:06:18.657 --> 00:06:20.794
<i>♪ Don't you want me? Oh ♪</i>

120
00:06:20.795 --> 00:06:26.171
[gasps] Oh. Bret.
please get drunk every night.

121
00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:27.975
[moaning]

122
00:06:28.911 --> 00:06:30.446
[panting]

123
00:06:31.516 --> 00:06:33.251
[both moaning]

124
00:06:33.252 --> 00:06:34.988
[♪ song ends]

125
00:06:34.989 --> 00:06:36.191
[birds chirping]

126
00:06:37.862 --> 00:06:41.101
-[Debbie chuckling]
-[inhales sharply]

127
00:06:41.102 --> 00:06:42.470
Hi. sexy.

128
00:06:43.640 --> 00:06:45.476
You were amazing last night.

129
00:06:46.178 --> 00:06:48.049
I was. wasn't I?

130
00:06:49.151 --> 00:06:50.554
Matt called.

131
00:06:52.592 --> 00:06:53.994
-Who?
-Matt.

132
00:06:54.729 --> 00:06:55.831
From school?

133
00:06:57.535 --> 00:06:59.070
What did he want?

134
00:06:59.071 --> 00:07:01.208
Oh. you were so knocked out.
I didn't wanna wake you.

135
00:07:02.678 --> 00:07:04.816
He said to stop calling.

136
00:07:05.384 --> 00:07:06.719
[♪ tense music playing]

137
00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:08.623
What's that supposed to mean?

138
00:07:08.624 --> 00:07:10.093
No idea. [chuckles]

139
00:07:12.732 --> 00:07:14.034
I'll see you tonight.

140
00:07:29.632 --> 00:07:32.103
[Bret] <i>One of the hallmarks
of the early 1980s</i>

141
00:07:32.104 --> 00:07:34.041
<i>for a young person
in Los Angeles</i>

142
00:07:34.475 --> 00:07:37.782
<i>was you had to survive things
to become an adult.</i>

143
00:07:39.786 --> 00:07:43.593
<i>Real-life boogeymen known
as serial killers were a threat.</i>

144
00:07:43.594 --> 00:07:44.728
[siren wailing]

145
00:07:44.729 --> 00:07:46.198
[Bret] <i>And so were cults.</i>

146
00:07:47.568 --> 00:07:48.603
[bird squawks]

147
00:07:50.808 --> 00:07:54.046
[Bret] <i>The cult that terrorized
Los Angeles in 1981.</i>

148
00:07:54.047 --> 00:07:56.552
<i>when I was a senior
in high school.</i>

149
00:07:56.553 --> 00:08:01.662
<i>was bloodthirsty. terrifying and
had similar habits to The Trawler.</i>

150
00:08:01.663 --> 00:08:02.831
[glass shatters]

151
00:08:02.832 --> 00:08:05.603
[Bret] <i>In fact.</i>

152
00:08:05.604 --> 00:08:08.418
<i>law enforcement would suspect that this
cult was involved in The Trawler murders</i>

153
00:08:08.442 --> 00:08:12.016
<i>and that the vicious ritualist
killings plaguing the city</i>

154
00:08:12.017 --> 00:08:15.623
<i>were done not by one member.
but by several.</i>

155
00:08:15.624 --> 00:08:17.661
[♪ eerie music playing]

156
00:08:25.276 --> 00:08:28.049
[door creaks]

157
00:08:30.588 --> 00:08:32.757
[Bret] <i>The city
had never truly recuperated</i>

158
00:08:32.758 --> 00:08:35.029
<i>from the Manson killings
a decade earlier.</i>

159
00:08:35.598 --> 00:08:37.901
<i>And like Charlie
and the Manson girls.</i>

160
00:08:37.902 --> 00:08:41.307
<i>the Riders of the Afterlife.
as they called themselves.</i>

161
00:08:41.308 --> 00:08:43.713
<i>reigned from Ojai
to the San Fernando Valley.</i>

162
00:08:43.714 --> 00:08:46.752
[cult members murmuring.
screaming]

163
00:08:46.753 --> 00:08:48.656
[Bret] <i>This group of young.</i>

164
00:08:48.657 --> 00:08:51.929
<i>barely-articulate hippies
formed out in the Mojave.</i>

165
00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:55.102
<i>acolytes of a leader
only referred to as Bruce.</i>

166
00:08:55.103 --> 00:08:58.643
<i>who turned out to be a high school
English teacher from Lancaster.</i>

167
00:08:58.644 --> 00:09:02.250
<i>fired due to sexual improprieties
with female students.</i>

168
00:09:02.919 --> 00:09:04.589
[exhales]

169
00:09:06.392 --> 00:09:10.032
[Bret] <i>The cult did drugs.
acid. tranquilizers</i>

170
00:09:10.033 --> 00:09:13.071
<i>and their activities
quickly accelerated that year</i>

171
00:09:13.072 --> 00:09:16.010
<i>as Bruce became more addicted
and messianic.</i>

172
00:09:16.011 --> 00:09:18.015
[screaming continues]

173
00:09:19.218 --> 00:09:21.689
Yeah.

174
00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:24.293
Well. maybe I should ask for the
recipe so that I can make it for you.

175
00:09:24.294 --> 00:09:25.763
Honey?

176
00:09:25.764 --> 00:09:27.233
[♪ ominous music playing]

177
00:09:30.306 --> 00:09:31.609
[partner 1] Oh. my God.

178
00:09:32.277 --> 00:09:33.613
Is that blood?

179
00:09:35.216 --> 00:09:37.086
[partner 2] Go inside
and call the police.

180
00:09:38.355 --> 00:09:41.295
[Bret] <i>Then came break-ins in
Hancock Park and Silver Lake.</i>

181
00:09:41.797 --> 00:09:44.100
<i>They wanted to unify
through fear.</i>

182
00:09:44.869 --> 00:09:47.206
<i>-And then things got worse.</i>
-[grunting]

183
00:09:47.207 --> 00:09:49.978
[Bret] <i>The home invasions
escalated to violence.</i>

184
00:09:49.979 --> 00:09:52.449
<i>The victims who survived
those early attacks</i>

185
00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:56.258
<i>said the intruder wore a black ski
mask and matching jeans and turtleneck.</i>

186
00:09:58.329 --> 00:10:00.399
<i>He was
a terrifying shape-shifter.</i>

187
00:10:06.378 --> 00:10:09.017
<i>And then
the first murder occurred.</i>

188
00:10:15.263 --> 00:10:16.733
[gasps]

189
00:10:17.502 --> 00:10:20.072
[news anchor 1] <i>...as authorities
continue to hunt for The Trawler.</i>

190
00:10:20.073 --> 00:10:23.879
<i>the serial killer targeting young
people throughout Los Angeles.</i>

191
00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:26.852
<i>Police fear The Trawler
will strike again.</i>

192
00:10:26.853 --> 00:10:31.127
<i>Police are warning residents
throughout Los Angeles to remain vigilant.</i>

193
00:10:31.128 --> 00:10:35.335
<i>A gruesome discovery in Brentwood tonight
after a home invasion turned deadly.</i>

194
00:10:35.336 --> 00:10:38.876
[Bret] <i>Between nightly news
reports of The Trawler murders.</i>

195
00:10:38.877 --> 00:10:41.281
<i>two other young people
were now missing.</i>

196
00:10:41.282 --> 00:10:44.420
<i>and then reports of the Riders
of the Afterlife attacks.</i>

197
00:10:44.421 --> 00:10:47.227
<i>The city was on edge
and so was I.</i>

198
00:10:51.435 --> 00:10:54.976
<i>Every night. I kept thinking
I heard someone in the house.</i>

199
00:10:55.578 --> 00:10:57.781
<i>I was at my desk working
on my novel.</i>

200
00:10:58.215 --> 00:11:00.419
<i>and whenever I stopped typing
I would feel a presence</i>

201
00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:02.925
<i>either lurking outside the house</i>

202
00:11:03.292 --> 00:11:04.928
<i>or somewhere within it.</i>

203
00:11:04.929 --> 00:11:06.699
[doorbell ringing]

204
00:11:11.175 --> 00:11:12.845
[doorbell continues ringing]

205
00:11:20.193 --> 00:11:22.262
[♪ eerie music playing]

206
00:11:22.263 --> 00:11:24.433
<i>A number of times
I thought I heard the doorbell</i>

207
00:11:24.434 --> 00:11:27.407
<i>or the chiming that announced
the garage doors opening.</i>

208
00:11:28.309 --> 00:11:31.816
<i>For weeks I crept through
the house clutching a weapon.</i>

209
00:12:09.057 --> 00:12:10.326
<i>But no one was there.</i>

210
00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:13.032
<i>Not yet.</i>

211
00:12:16.071 --> 00:12:17.941
<i>But I could tell
they were coming.</i>

212
00:12:17.942 --> 00:12:19.377
[♪ sinister music plays]

213
00:13:02.297 --> 00:13:04.835
[sighs] Goddamn it. Liz.

214
00:13:05.436 --> 00:13:07.607
[grunts] Mom!

215
00:13:07.608 --> 00:13:09.210
[♪ "Déjà Vu" playing]

216
00:13:09.211 --> 00:13:10.279
Mom!

217
00:13:11.448 --> 00:13:13.987
<i>♪ Long ago ♪</i>

218
00:13:16.458 --> 00:13:19.097
<i>♪ How can it be? ♪</i>

219
00:13:21.201 --> 00:13:22.904
That's my Lancôme.

220
00:13:22.905 --> 00:13:25.008
You're not allowed
to wear eye shadow at school.

221
00:13:25.009 --> 00:13:26.277
I'm going out.

222
00:13:26.278 --> 00:13:27.614
I'm almost done.

223
00:13:27.615 --> 00:13:29.918
[Debbie breathes deeply]

224
00:13:29.919 --> 00:13:32.490
I'm going to La Scala with
Joanie Carson and Jackie Collins.

225
00:13:34.595 --> 00:13:37.199
Going out with Bret
tonight again? [huffs]

226
00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:39.170
Yes. Mother. we're in love.

227
00:13:39.639 --> 00:13:43.311
Being with each other whenever you can
is what being in love looks like. Remember?

228
00:13:43.312 --> 00:13:46.250
You wanna look good
for your man. I get it.

229
00:13:46.251 --> 00:13:49.157
[breathes deeply] Oh. honey.

230
00:13:49.959 --> 00:13:51.261
Men. [scoffs]

231
00:13:52.030 --> 00:13:55.302
All your meaningless flirtations
you think will get you somewhere

232
00:13:55.303 --> 00:13:57.339
-and make you happy.
-Just give me the compact

233
00:13:57.340 --> 00:13:58.877
and have another Chablis. Mom.

234
00:14:02.083 --> 00:14:03.919
There's just so much
you don't know about them.

235
00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:05.489
There's just so much
